.alert.alert-light.border
  %h3.fw-semibold.mb-2 Goal of this page
  %p.mb-3
    During the HR-led talent-planning ritual (about every couple of months), record a keeper-test stance for each person on a manager's team — so the question is seat fit, not how painful hiring would be.

  %h3.fw-semibold.mb-2 Context
  %p.mb-2
    OurGruuv is built for transparency. Talent Density is a deliberate exception: employees are told this ritual exists, and
    %strong nobody ever sees their own stance
    — not even with manage-employment permission.
  %p.mb-3
    Magically ramped is the one cheat: ignore hiring, coverage, and ramp pain. The seat stays filled either way. I'd do nothing should be most people. I'd take the swap and I'd work to avoid the swap are both rare. Taking the swap is often the kind thing (good person, better seat elsewhere).

  %h3.fw-semibold.mb-2 Specifics of this page
  %h5.fw-semibold.mb-2 The question
  = render "organizations/talent_density/prompt"

  %h5.fw-semibold.mb-2 The three choices
  = render "organizations/talent_density/rubric_table"

  %h5.fw-semibold.mb-2 Who you see
  %ul.mb-3
    %li Pick a manager — yourself, or any manager in your hierarchy (same idea as health pages).
    %li
      The list is that manager's
      %strong current direct reports
      only, in one bulk page.
    %li People with manage-employment can pick any manager in the company.
    %li Your own row is never shown, including when you open your manager's team.

  %h5.fw-semibold.mb-2 Matrices
  %p.mb-3
    MgrStance+Rating Matrix plots keeper stance against last finalized position. Guidance+Rating Matrix plots actual overall against assignment-energy guidance. Filters are shared (manager, directs vs hierarchy, people to exclude).

  %h5.fw-semibold.mb-2 Saving and history
  %ul.mb-0
    %li Saving overwrites the current stance and notes. Change history (who changed what) is on each person via PaperTrail.
    %li This is a living ledger for the ritual — not a locked cycle or a performance score the employee can open.
